Package: org.webosarchive.v8fix
Version: 1.0.1
Depends:
Section: System
Architecture: all
Maintainer: webOS Archive
Description: Fix Enyo 2 apps on webOS 2.1.0 (V8 compiler bug)
Source: { "Type":"Application", "Feed":"WOSA Modernize", "Category":"Modernize", "LastUpdated":"1790954144", "Title":"V8 Fix for webOS 2.1.0", "FullDescription":"<b>For webOS 2.1.0 only</b> (Palm Pre 2, or a Pre / Pre Plus meta-doctored to 2.1.0). It does nothing on any other version.<br><br>Makes Enyo 2 apps such as Preware 2 display and work. The JavaScript engine in webOS 2.1.0 has a code generation bug that breaks minified Enyo 2: the app opens, but its screens stay broken or never finish loading. This package switches the engine that runs apps to its full code generator, which does not have the bug, by adding --always_full_compiler to the JavaScript flags in /etc/palm/browser.conf. Before changing anything it checks the webOS version and tests the device for the bug. The web browser is not changed.<br><br>Install it with the original Preware or WebOS Quick Install (Preware 2 needs this fix before it can display), then restart Luna. Remove it from Preware: the flag is taken out again. No other packages are needed.", "PostInstallFlags":"RestartLuna", "PostUpdateFlags":"RestartLuna", "PostRemoveFlags":"RestartLuna" }
